    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and reworks everything that keys off the household. All in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (plus doc updates in `openapi.yml`):\n\n**`householdIdFor` / `householdKey`** \u2014 now keyed on `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`. The id is the first **12 hex chars** of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, where the last name is normalized (whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased) exactly as before. An owner with no postcode belongs to no household (`null`). Dropped the old `HH-`/16-char format.\n\n**`assignHousehold`** \u2014 now assigns the deterministic id to *every* new owner (with a postcode) unconditionally, rather than only when `sharesHousehold` was set. Removed the `linkHouseholdMates`/`findHouseholdMates` back-filling machinery, which is obsolete now that the id is deterministic (owners sharing lastName+postcode automatically converge on the same value).\n\n**`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 now a **household duplicate** check: if any existing owner already carries the same computed `householdId`, the new owner is rejected with **409**. `sharesHousehold` bypasses the block (its only remaining role), so a declared member is created instead. Owners without a postcode have no household and are never household duplicates.\n\n**`applyPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate (\"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate\").\n\n**`countHouseholdMembers`** (the household-size input) already keyed off `householdId`, so it now naturally reflects the `(lastName, postcode)` grouping.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) and the full build pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
